    <sys:String x:Key="RecordingHelpTitle">Recording &amp; Playback Help</sys:String><sys:String x:Key="RecordingHelpText">With no selection, the global hotkey starts recording. With a selection, it starts playback. Press it again while running to stop.&#10;&#10;The first row contains controls. Recording has Start, Pause/Resume and Stop: pausing suspends capture and timing, resuming appends to this recording, and stopping ends and saves the captured actions. During playback, Start playback becomes Stop playback. Starting again after a stop begins with the first action.&#10;&#10;The second row shows status, action progress and elapsed time on the left. Hover for the complete loop count and error details. Actions include pointer movement, presses and releases; one click may contain several actions.&#10;&#10;Elapsed is hours:minutes:seconds.tenths. Pauses are excluded; loop intervals are included. The result remains after stopping or completing and resets when another recording is selected.&#10;&#10;On the right, adjust the speed slider (0.5–5× in 0.1 steps), loop count, infinite looping and loop interval. These options are unavailable during a run. More on each card contains hotkey, optimize, rename and delete actions. Standard privileges cannot control elevated windows.</sys:String>
